age](https://astropy-regions.readthedocs.io/en/stable/compound.html) but for `SpectralRegion` in specutils.

Motivation: Currently [jdaviz has to maintain complicated and recursive logic to turn composite subsets in glue into SpectralRegion[(https://github.com/spacetelescope/jdaviz/blob/05e9afb0fdc11d062e52b483b11ee5ac1e8577ec/jdaviz/app.py#L1126). In addition to maintenance burden, such functionality would be indefinitely more useful even to non-Jdaviz users if implemented natively in specutils.

When this exists here, Jdaviz can then retire the complicated code and add [proper translators to glue-astronomy](https://github.com/glue-viz/glue-astronomy/blob/main/glue_astronomy/translators/spectrum1d.py) because then `glue` operators will [combine them natively via operator overloading](https://github.com/glue-viz/glue/blob/0c8f5e88c66c513b2132a123b11fc6bbc72b7f1d/glue/core/subset_group.py#L207).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/specutils/issues/1205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/astropy/specutils/issues/1205/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}}

